RESULT
PASS: The standalone Android app installed a hash-checked Android/Bionic ARM64
OpenJDK from APK assets, ran Java 21 and javac, launched the Flutter-generated
Gradle wrapper, downloaded and unpacked Gradle 9.1.0, ran it on the Android
ARM64 JVM, then launched it again with offline mode from the private cache. A
warm app relaunch reused the JDK and Gradle distribution.

LIMIT OF THIS RESULT
The Gradle proof runs `--version`; it does not yet configure the generated
Flutter Android build, resolve AGP/Kotlin build plugins, compile Java/Kotlin,
or produce an APK. The next bundle must add Flutter's Gradle plugin sources, an
Android SDK platform, Android build-tool JARs, and ARM64/Bionic AAPT2. The
current executable-from-private-storage design also still depends on the
research app's legacy targetSdk 28 and is not the final production packaging
model.
